{%- comment -%}
  ============================================================
  Product card
  ============================================================

  ONE card, rendered by every grid that shows products: Best sellers, You
  may also like, and anything added later. It lived inside sp-bestsellers
  until a second grid needed it, and a copied card is a card that drifts —
  the next change to the hover swap or the rating rule would have had to be
  made twice, and would have been made once.

  Called as:

      {% render 'sp-product-card',
         p: product,
         card: settings,          a settings object, or the section's own
         index: forloop.index0,
         placeholder: true %}       draws an empty card, see below

  `placeholder` exists because a snippet cannot see the collection the
  section was pointed at. Best sellers renders a grid of empty cards when its
  collection is unset or empty — a section that is present but blank is the
  hardest kind to debug — and it has to say so explicitly.

  `card` carries the display options the grid was configured with, so the
  snippet reads card.show_rating rather than section.settings.show_rating and
  therefore never depends on which section is rendering it.

  Everything shown is the shop's own data. The rating comes only from the
  reviews metafield a review app writes — never derived from the product id.
  A rating no customer gave is a fabricated review, and publishing one is an
  offence under the DMCC Act 2024.
  ============================================================
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign v = p.selected_or_first_available_variant

assign on_sale = false
if v.compare_at_price > v.price
  assign on_sale = true
endif

comment
  One variant means quick add is unambiguous. More than one and the
  shopper has a choice to make, so send them to make it.
endcomment
assign single = false
if p.variants.size == 1 and v.available
  assign single = true
endif

comment
  Second media for the hover swap. Skipped when the product only
  has one image, so the card does not cross-fade to itself.
endcomment
assign hover_media = blank
if p.media.size > 1
  for m in p.media
    if m.id == p.featured_media.id
      continue
    endif
    assign hover_media = m
    break
  endfor
endif

comment
  The chip names where the piece sits. Product type first because
  a merchant sets it deliberately; the first collection is the
  fallback because every product has one.
endcomment
comment
  The colour option, found by name wherever it sits in the option
  list, so Size / Colour and Colour / Size both work.
endcomment
assign colour_opt = blank
for option in p.options_with_values
  assign nm = option.name | downcase
  if nm contains 'color' or nm contains 'colour' or nm contains 'fabric' or nm contains 'finish' or nm contains 'shade'
    assign colour_opt = option
    break
  endif
endfor

assign save_pct = 0
if on_sale
  assign save_pct = v.compare_at_price | minus: v.price | times: 100.0 | divided_by: v.compare_at_price | round
endif

comment
  One line about the piece: a short_description metafield if the
  merchant keeps one, otherwise the opening of the description.
endcomment
assign blurb = p.metafields.custom.short_description.value | default: p.metafields.custom.short_description
if blurb == blank
  assign blurb = p.description | strip_html | truncate: 72
endif

comment
  Rating comes only from a real reviews metafield, the one review
  apps write. It is never derived from the product id: a rating no
  customer gave is a fabricated review, and publishing one is an
  offence under the DMCC Act 2024.
endcomment
assign rating = p.metafields.reviews.rating.value
assign rating_count = p.metafields.reviews.rating_count
assign rating_pct = 0
if rating != blank
  assign rating_pct = rating.rating | times: 1.0 | divided_by: 5.0 | times: 100
endif
        -%}
<li class="sp-bs__item" style="--i: {{ index | default: 0 }};" data-sp-reveal>
  {%- if placeholder -%}
    <div class="sp-bs__card sp-bs__card--ph">
      <div class="sp-bs__frame">
        <span class="sp-bs__media"><span class="sp-bs__ph" aria-hidden="true"></span></span>
      </div>
      <span class="sp-bs__body">
        <span class="sp-bs__title">Product</span>
        <span class="sp-bs__price"><span class="sp-bs__now">&mdash;</span></span>
      </span>
    </div>
  {%- else -%}
    <div class="sp-bs__card{% if hover_media != blank %} has-swap{% endif %}">
      <div class="sp-bs__frame" data-sp-tilt>
        <a class="sp-bs__media" href="{{ p.url }}" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="sp-bs__stack">
          {%- if p.featured_media != blank -%}
            {%- assign p_alt = p.featured_media.alt | default: p.title -%}
            {{
              p.featured_media
              | image_url: width: 900
              | image_tag:
                class: 'sp-bs__img sp-bs__img--front',
                widths: '250, 400, 600, 900',
                sizes: '(min-width: 1100px) 24vw, (min-width: 750px) 45vw, 90vw',
                loading: 'lazy',
                alt: p_alt
            }}
          {%- else -%}
            <span class="sp-bs__ph" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if hover_media != blank -%}
            {%- assign h_alt = '' -%}
            {{
              hover_media
              | image_url: width: 900
              | image_tag:
                class: 'sp-bs__img sp-bs__img--back',
                widths: '250, 400, 600, 900',
                sizes: '(min-width: 1100px) 24vw, (min-width: 750px) 45vw, 90vw',
                loading: 'lazy',
                alt: h_alt
            }}
          {%- endif -%}

          <span class="sp-bs__shadow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </span>

        {%- if on_sale -%}
          <span class="sp-bs__badge">&minus;{{ save_pct }}%</span>
        {%- endif -%}
        </a>

        {%- if card.show_wishlist -%}
          <button
            type="button"
            class="sp-bs__wish"
            data-sp-wish="{{ p.id }}"
            data-sp-wish-handle="{{ p.handle }}"
            aria-pressed="false"
            aria-label="{{ card.wish_label | default: 'Save for later' | escape }}"
          >
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="17" height="17" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M12 20s-7-4.6-7-9.3A4.2 4.2 0 0 1 12 8a4.2 4.2 0 0 1 7 2.7C19 15.4 12 20 12 20Z" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            </svg>
          </button>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      <div class="sp-bs__body">
        <div class="sp-bs__row">
          <h3 class="sp-bs__title"><a href="{{ p.url }}">{{ p.title | escape }}</a></h3>
          <span class="sp-bs__prices">
            <span class="sp-bs__pill">{{ v.price | money }}</span>
            {%- if on_sale -%}
              <s class="sp-bs__was">{{ v.compare_at_price | money }}</s>
            {%- endif -%}
          </span>
        </div>

        {%- if card.show_rating -%}
          <p class="sp-bs__rating">
            <span class="sp-bs__stars" style="--pct: {{ rating_pct }}%" role="img" aria-label="Rated {{ rating.rating }} out of 5">
              <span class="sp-bs__stars-track" aria-hidden="true">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</span>
              <span class="sp-bs__stars-fill" aria-hidden="true">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</span>
            </span>
            {%- if rating != blank -%}
              <span class="sp-bs__rating-num">{{ rating.rating }}</span>
              {%- if rating_count != blank -%}
                <span class="sp-bs__rating-count">({{ rating_count }})</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- else -%}
              <span class="sp-bs__rating-none">{{ card.no_reviews_label | default: 'No reviews yet' | escape }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if blurb != blank and card.show_blurb -%}
          <p class="sp-bs__blurb">{{ blurb | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if colour_opt != blank and card.show_colours -%}
          <ul class="sp-bs__colours" role="list" aria-label="{{ colour_opt.name | escape }}">
            {%- for value in colour_opt.values limit: card.colour_limit -%}
              {%- liquid
                comment
                  Shopify's own swatch where the merchant set one,
                  otherwise the value name used as a CSS colour. A name
                  CSS cannot parse falls through to the tone underneath,
                  so a swatch is never invisible.
                endcomment
                assign sw = value.swatch.color
                if sw == blank
                  assign sw = value | downcase | split: ' ' | last
                endif
              -%}
              <li class="sp-bs__colour" style="--sw: {{ sw }};" title="{{ value | escape }}">
                <span class="visually-hidden">{{ value | escape }}</span>
              </li>
            {%- endfor -%}
            {%- assign extra = colour_opt.values.size | minus: card.colour_limit -%}
            {%- if extra > 0 -%}
              <li class="sp-bs__colour-more">+{{ extra }}</li>
            {%- endif -%}
          </ul>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="sp-bs__action">
          {%- if single -%}
            {%- form 'product', p, class: 'sp-bs__form', novalidate: 'novalidate' -%}
              <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ v.id }}">
              <button type="submit" class="sp-bs__add" data-sp-quickadd>
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M7 8h12l-1.2 8.2a1.5 1.5 0 0 1-1.5 1.3H9.4a1.5 1.5 0 0 1-1.5-1.25L6.2 5.4A1 1 0 0 0 5.2 4.5H3.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                  <circle cx="10" cy="20" r="1.15" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/>
                  <circle cx="17" cy="20" r="1.15" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/>
                </svg>
                <span>{{ card.add_label | default: 'Add To Cart' | escape }}</span>
              </button>
            {%- endform -%}
          {%- else -%}
            <a
              class="sp-bs__add sp-bs__add--options"
              href="{{ p.url }}"
              {% if card.quick_view and v.available %}data-sp-quickview{% endif %}
            >
              <span>
                {%- if v.available -%}
                  {{ card.options_label | default: 'Choose options' | escape }}
                {%- else -%}
                  {{ 'products.product.sold_out' | t }}
                {%- endif -%}
              </span>
            </a>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</li>
